@* The split (BACKBAR-5, handoff pages 05–06 and 13–14): her scene as half the screen with a line
   on it, and the working side beside — Login, the wizard, Join and the auth error page. One
   component so four screens do not each re-spell where she stands.

   Her panel keeps its night ground in BOTH themes: the illustration is a night bar scene and carries
   its own light. Only the working side follows the theme. That is the one intentional exception to
   the theme swap, and it is drawn here once rather than remembered four times.

   Her scene carries her and her line, and nothing else. The handoff put the wordmark in its top
   corner, which at every width is over her face; the working side carries the brand instead, so the
   pages that borrow the split put the lockup there themselves (Login, Join, the auth error page). *@

<div class="split @(Warm ? "split-warm" : null) @(Compact ? "split-compact" : null) @(Full ? "split-full" : null)">
    <div class="split-scene">
        <img class="split-scene-art" src="_content/JiggerJot.Shared.Ui/brand/marga_scene_512.png"
             alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="512" height="512" />
        <div class="split-scene-text">
            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Aside))
            {
                <span class="split-eyebrow">@Aside</span>
            }
            <p class="split-line font-display">@Line</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="split-panel">
        @ChildContent
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The sentence on the scene — hers, or the error copy on the auth error page.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Line { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The small brass label above the line ("Marga · behind the bar"); none when absent.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Aside { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The wizard's warm base (#2A1A12) under the gradient rather than the login's night.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Warm { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A shorter scene, for the small screens (join, auth error) that have little beside it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Compact { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Edge to edge and the viewport's full height, with the working side a fixed 440px pane at
    /// <c>lg</c> and her scene taking the rest — the sibling apps' sign-in shape. Login only: the
    /// wizard sits under the app header, and Join and the auth error page have one paragraph beside her.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Full { get; set; }

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
